\frac{1}{Z} = \frac{1}{n_e \cdot n_i \cdot \lambda_+} + \frac{1}{n_e \cdot n_i \cdot \lambda_-}
where $Z$ is the equivalent conductance, $n_e$ and $n_i$ are the concentrations of the cations and anions, and $\lambda_+$ and $\lambda_-$ are the conductivities of the cations and anions, respectively. We are given that $Z = 0.0412$ and $t_+ = 0.825$. We can solve for $\lambda_+$ and $\lambda_-$.
\frac{1}{0.0412} = \frac{1}{0.825 \cdot n_e \cdot n_i} + \frac{1}{0.825 \cdot n_e \cdot n_i}
\Rightarrow n_e \cdot n_i = \frac{0.0412}{0.0412 - 2 \cdot 0.825}
\Rightarrow n_e \cdot n_i = 0.00721
\Rightarrow \lambda_+ = \frac{0.00721}{0.825}
\Rightarrow \lambda_+ = 0.00825
\Rightarrow \lambda_- = 0.0412 - \lambda_+ = 0.03399
The answer is (H).
